# Module: Packaging

**Purpose:** Decide how convention packages compose and extend one another.

## Decision: Extensions Reference Their Base Package

**Status:** Adopted

**Context:** Some conventions may specialize a broader concern. Copying base
documents into an extending package would create drift, while treating every
package as unrelated would lose the relationship needed by consumers.

**Decision:**

A package may explicitly extend another package. The package
record names its base package, and every extending convention file contains a
mandatory reading section pointing to the parent package

Example for `@noodlestan/conventions-solidjs` (extends `@noodlestan/conventions-jsx`):

```text
:READ `@noodlestan/conventions-jsx/`
```

The child file describes only additions or constraints. It does not copy the
base package's documents; consumers resolve the base package plus the
extension.
